invariant: INV-75
file: proof/run.sh
catches: test/prove-status-check.sh
reason: inflight counts a job as alive while kill -0 finds its process
  id, whether or not the job wrote its status. Once a long-lived process
  takes a reused id, the admission loop waits for a job that already
  ended, and at CPU_CAP such entries stop the run. The check runs with
  kill -0 finding every process alive and one job at a time, and
  requires the run to end in 30 s.

--- old
        if [ ! -f "$LOGDIR/${rest#*:}.rc" ] && kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null; then
--- new
        if kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null; then
